OL,3,GNEWSA'The greatest privilege' - Dad
OL,4,Adonates organs to son
OL,5,
OL,6,FA six-year-old boy has received part of
OL,7,Fhis dad's liver and bowel after he
OL,8,Fbecame in desperate need of a
OL,9,Ftransplant.
OL,11,FHarry, from Cambridge, was born with an
OL,12,Fabnormality of the bowel that can cut
OL,13,Foff the blood supply, and also
OL,14,Fdeveloped intestinal failure-associated
OL,15,Fliver disease.
OL,17,FHis parents knew he would probably need
OL,18,Fa bowel transplant at some point, but
OL,19,Fit came "much sooner than we ever
OL,20,Fimagined", said his mum Annie.
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
